9. Never fabricate successful API responses, delivery statuses, GPS positions, courier availability, payments, or notification delivery.
10. Never consider a frontend-only implementation to be a functional backend feature.
11. Never expose service-role keys, private credentials, database secrets, payment secrets, or privileged operations in the client.
12. Do not create fake courier activity, fake live maps, fake dispatch success, or fake notifications in production.
13. Use the existing project architecture wherever possible.
14. If a required service is not configured, implement its integration structure safely and clearly identify the missing configuration.
15. Do not stop after producing a plan. After the audit, proceed with implementation in controlled phases, testing each phase.
