6. COURIER AVAILABILITY AND GPS

A courier is not available merely because their account exists.

Implement a reliable courier availability model.

Possible statuses:

* OFFLINE
* ONLINE
* AVAILABLE
* OFFER_PENDING
* ASSIGNED
* PICKUP_IN_PROGRESS
* DELIVERY_IN_PROGRESS
* TEMPORARILY_UNAVAILABLE
* SUSPENDED

Adapt these statuses to the existing architecture.

Courier availability requirements

A courier must satisfy all applicable conditions:

* Approved account
* Valid operational city
* Online status
* Valid recent GPS position
* GPS accuracy within acceptable limits
* Compatible vehicle
* Eligible parcel category
* Not suspended
* Not overloaded
* Not blocked by operational restrictions
* Not already assigned beyond permitted capacity

GPS freshness

A stale GPS location must not be treated as a live courier position.

Store:

* Latitude
* Longitude
* Timestamp
* Accuracy
* Heading, if available
* Speed, if available
* Device identifier, if appropriate and privacy-compliant

Define configurable location-freshness thresholds.

If a courier’s location is outdated:

* Exclude the courier from proximity dispatch or penalize eligibility.
* Do not display the courier as accurately positioned.
* Do not use stale coordinates as a live tracking position.

GPS privacy

Location tracking must:

* Operate only when necessary.
* Respect courier service status.
* Stop or reduce tracking when the courier is offline.
* Be restricted to authorized users.
* Avoid unnecessary historical location retention.
* Protect customer and courier location data.
* Never expose a courier’s private location to unrelated users.

